Add sys/wait.h for WIFEXITED, WEXITSTATUS, WIFSIGNALED and WTERMSIG.

Upstream relies on these macros arriving indirectly through another header,
which happens to hold on glibc.  POSIX places them in <sys/wait.h>, and MIU
Darwin's headers follow that placement, so the file does not compile without
the explicit include.

The same omission is patched in the OpenBSD port, which is a fair sign the
include is simply missing upstream rather than being a quirk of either system.

--- src/ptyxis-tab.c.orig
+++ src/ptyxis-tab.c
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <glib/gi18n.h>

 #include <cairo.h>
+#include <sys/wait.h>

 #ifdef __linux__
 # include <libportal/portal.h>
